 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? I usually recommend seven days for quick oil paints like oil pastels. Longer drying time, but it' worth checking the oil paint you used because some people varnish after just few days. That's a good timeframe. Just pop it in the living room and look at it lot. Then dash downstairs just before leaving. You can use a thin layer of lacquer spray if you' in a rush. It' only give you a few hours of protection though. Brush strokes will still show, and the oil smell will still be there. At seven days, both are barely noticeable.",
